S.world={lvl:1,label:"The world",spot:"340px 170px",
intro:{name:"The wider world",car:"Cars are built in factories, sold through showrooms and dealerships, fuelled at stations, kept in garages, serviced by mechanics and policed by the Highway Code.",ai:"Agentic AI has the same chain. Click a place to see who does what, or click Zoom in to go back to the car on the road.",p:[]},
items:[
It("w1","Factories",null,90,40,"Where engines are built.","Model labs train the models. Building one takes huge amounts of data and computing power, so only a few organisations do it.",["Anthropic","OpenAI","Google DeepMind","Meta","Mistral","DeepSeek"]),
It("w2","Coachbuilders",null,250,40,"Firms that build the body for someone else\u2019s engine.","Products that wrap a model in a harness: the interface, tools and loop. Many let you choose or swap the engine.",["Cursor","Lovable","Replit"]),
It("w3","Dealerships",null,420,40,"Resell engines from several makers, with the paperwork a big buyer needs.","Cloud platforms that offer several models behind one account, with billing, security and permissions.",["Amazon Bedrock","Microsoft Foundry","Google Cloud"]),
It("w4","Showrooms",null,585,40,"Where you try and buy the finished car.","Consumer apps where you meet the model and the harness together.",["Claude app","ChatGPT","Gemini app","Microsoft Copilot"]),
