intro:{name:"Under the bonnet: the model",car:"The engine is built at a factory, comes in sizes, is tuned for a job and tested on a dyno.",ai:"This is the model. Everything here is about the engine itself, before any cabin, tools or connections. Pick a part to see what it means.",p:["Anthropic Claude","OpenAI GPT","Google Gemini","Mistral","Meta Llama","DeepSeek"]},
items:[
It("b1","Pre-training",null,110,62,"Building the engine at the factory.","Training on a vast pile of text so the model learns language and general knowledge. It takes months and enormous computing power.",["Anthropic","OpenAI","Google DeepMind","Meta","Mistral","DeepSeek"]),
It("b2","Model tiers",null,290,62,"Engine sizes: small and economical, mid-range, top performance.","Small, fast models for simple repeatable jobs, mid-tier for everyday work, top-tier for the hardest problems. Bigger usually means slower and dearer.",["Claude Haiku, Sonnet and Opus","Small-to-large lines from OpenAI and Google"]),
It("b3","Open or closed weights",null,490,62,"A sealed engine you rent, or a blueprint you can build yourself.","Weights are the learned settings inside a model. Closed: you use it through the maker\u2019s API. Open weights: you can download it and run it yourself, though licences vary.",["Closed: Claude, GPT, Gemini","Open weights: Llama, Mistral, DeepSeek, Qwen"]),
It("b4","Parameters",null,315,182,"How many tuned parts the engine has.","Parameters are the adjustable numbers set during training. More usually means more capable and more costly to run. Most closed makers do not publish the count.",["Rarely published by closed makers"]),
